gdate: disable format-nonliteral warning around g_date_strftime

GCC 14 diagnoses the dynamic format passed to strftime() as an error when
GLib enables -Werror=format-nonliteral.  Keep the warning disabled for the
whole function without changing its runtime behavior.

Backported from Python-independent GLib compatibility fixes:
https://github.com/frida/pkg-config/blob/master/glib-patches/gcc-format-nonliteral-2.patch

Adapted for glib-2.44.1.

Signed-off-by: jeep <jeep@local>

--- glib-2.44.1.orig/glib/gdate.c	2014-12-20 05:49:48.000000000 +0800
+++ glib-2.44.1/glib/gdate.c	2026-10-01 19:21:28.116137041 +0800
@@ -2439,6 +2439,9 @@
  *
  * Returns: number of characters written to the buffer, or 0 the buffer was too small
  */
+#pragma GCC diagnostic push
+#pragma GCC diagnostic ignored "-Wformat-nonliteral"
+
 gsize     
 g_date_strftime (gchar       *s, 
                  gsize        slen, 
@@ -2549,3 +2552,5 @@
   return retval;
 #endif
 }
+
+#pragma GCC diagnostic pop
